{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "GWDOColumnState",
    "description": "The column state GWDO builds before it knows anything about the orography: the thermodynamic profile, the earth-relative wind, the three orography-referenced level indices, the pressure-weighted low-level means, the projected wind speed along the low-level flow, and the layer Richardson number and squared Brunt-Vaisala frequency -- together with the six-way gate `ldrag` that switches the whole scheme off in a column. This is lines 249-459 of `phys/physics_mmm/bl_gwdo.F90` (WRF 4.8, NCAR/MMM-physics CCPP kernel `bl_gwdo_run`, the Hong et al. 2025 revision), which every later stage reads and none of which mentions the sub-grid orography statistics beyond the standard deviation `var` and the maximum height `omax` = ELVMAX.\n\nThe column is a consumer-supplied read, not owned state: `u`, `v`, `T`, `q_v`, the two pressure profiles, the Exner function and the layer heights all enter as plain algebraic reads of `input_*` rewrite targets and every product is an OBSERVED, so mounting this component adds no ODE state to a coupled document and cannot integrate a private copy of a column the document is also advancing.\n\nThe vertical coordinate is the COLUMN MASS above the surface, ze[k] = (p_i[1] - p_i[k])/g in kg/m^2, monotone increasing with the lev index. That is the coordinate GWDO's own vertical operator is taken with respect to -- the stress divergence is -g dtau/dp -- so the EarthSciDiscretizations `column_nonuniform_1d` grid is mounted on it, and the layer measure dz it derives IS del/g. The geometric heights zl enter separately as data, because that is how WRF supplies them (layer centres only, with no interface heights); they are used only by the three threshold searches and by the shear denominator, never as a control volume.\n\nRICHARDSON NUMBER, the quantity FORTRAN_BUGS N85 is about. `usqj` here is the RAW layer Richardson number for k >= kref and the pressure-weighted low-level average for k < kref, exactly as the Fortran overwrites level 1 with the average and then floods it down through kref-1. The wave-saturation stage compares it against ric = 0.25 and then evaluates 2 sqrt(temc) - temc with temc = 2 + 1/sqrt(Ri), which vanishes at that same 0.25; the amplification that produces is traced in `wave_saturation.esm` and in the tolerance of every test that reaches it.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "wrf",
      "gravity-wave-drag",
      "gwdo",
      "orography",
      "richardson-number",
      "column"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Hong, S.-Y., and co-authors (2025). Revision of the orographic gravity wave drag parameterization in the KIAPS Integrated Model. Wea. Forecasting."
      },
      {
        "citation": "Choi, H.-J., and S.-Y. Hong (2015). An updated subgrid orographic parameterization for global atmospheric forecast models. J. Geophys. Res. Atmos. 120, 12445-12457.",
        "doi": "10.1002/2015JD024230"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Kim, Y.-J., and A. Arakawa (1995). Improvement of orographic gravity wave parameterization using a mesoscale gravity wave model. J. Atmos. Sci. 52, 1875-1902.",
        "doi": "10.1175/1520-0469(1995)052<1875:IOOGWP>2.0.CO;2"
      },
      {
        "citation": "NCAR/MMM-physics bl_gwdo.F90 at commit 52cfbd7 (WRF 4.8 phys/physics_mmm submodule)."
      }
    ]
  },
  "metaparameters": {
    "NLEV": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 50,
      "description": "Number of model layers (WRF kte); 50 is the Last Chance Gulch d01 reference column of data/eqwefic/notes/gwdo_real_reference_run.md. Bound at the mount edge and passed down to the imported grid and template library."
    }
  },
  "models": {
    "GWDOColumnState": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "${ESD_ROOT}/grids/column_nonuniform_1d/grid.esm",
          "bindings": {
            "NLEV": "NLEV"
          }
        },
        {
          "ref": "./gwdo_templates.esm",
          "bindings": {
            "NLEV": "NLEV"
          }
        }
      ],
      "subsystems": {
        "wrf": {
          "ref": "../../../lib/wrf_constants.esm"
        },
        "par": {
          "ref": "./gwdo_parameters.esm"
        }
      },
      "variables": {
        "uproj": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m/s",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Projection-relative zonal wind on the model grid (WRF `uproj`, the rotated wind the dynamics carries)."
        },
        "vproj": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m/s",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Projection-relative meridional wind on the model grid (WRF `vproj`)."
        },
        "T": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Layer temperature."
        },
        "qv": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/kg",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Water-vapour mixing ratio."
        },
        "prsi": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "Pa",
          "shape": [
            "lev_nodes"
          ],
          "description": "Pressure at the NLEV+1 layer interfaces, decreasing with the lev index; prsi[1] is the surface."
        },
        "prsl": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "Pa",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Pressure at the layer mid-points."
        },
        "prslk": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Exner function (p/p00)^(R_d/cp) at the layer mid-points, WRF's `pi3d`."
        },
        "zl": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Geometric height of the layer mid-points above SEA level. GWDO compares it against ELVMAX, which is also above sea level (the comment at bl_gwdo.F90:284 records that this differs from the KIM/UFS convention, where both are above the model surface)."
        },
        "sina": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Sine of the map-rotation angle between the model grid and earth coordinates."
        },
        "cosa": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Cosine of the map-rotation angle."
        },
        "var": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "description": "Standard deviation of the sub-grid orography (WPS `VAR`)."
        },
        "omax": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "description": "Maximum sub-grid orographic height above sea level (WPS `ELVMAX`). WPS 4.3 does not write this field, and a run without it has omax = 0 everywhere, which the `omax <= hmt_min` gate below turns into silent zero drag at every point (FORTRAN_BUGS B17)."
        },
        "ze": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/m^2",
          "shape": [
            "lev_nodes"
          ],
          "description": "The column's vertical coordinate for the finite-volume operators: the air mass per unit area below each interface, (prsi[1] - prsi[k])/g, zero at the surface and increasing upward."
        },
        "dz": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/m^2",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Layer measure of the column_nonuniform_1d grid, derived from ze by the grid's own `column_cell_thickness` template: the layer mass per unit area del/g. Every rule on this grid reads it by this bare name."
        },
        "zc": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/m^2",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Layer mid-points of the mass coordinate, derived from ze by the grid's `column_cell_center` template. Part of the grid's keyed-factor contract; GWDO's own operators use only dz."
        },
        "del": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "Pa",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Positive pressure thickness of each layer, prsi[k] - prsi[k+1]."
        },
        "vtj": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Virtual temperature T (1 + eps_1 q_v)."
        },
        "vtk": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Virtual potential temperature, vtj divided by the Exner function."
        },
        "rho": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/m^3",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Air density from the ideal gas law with the virtual temperature."
        },
        "u1": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m/s",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Earth-relative zonal wind, uproj cosa - vproj sina."
        },
        "v1": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m/s",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Earth-relative meridional wind, uproj sina + vproj cosa."
        },
        "dzg": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Geometric distance between the mid-points of layers k and k+1, zl[k+1] - zl[k]: the length the Richardson number's shear and lapse rate are taken over. Element NLEV has no layer above it; it is set to 1 m so that the reciprocals below are finite, and the conditional that guards every use of it discards the value."
        },
        "dw2": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m^2/s^2",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Squared vector wind difference across the interface k+1/2, (u[k]-u[k+1])^2 + (v[k]-v[k+1])^2, zero at NLEV."
        },
        "zref": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "description": "Depth of the wave-launch layer, 2 var."
        },
        "kgwdmax": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Highest admissible reference level, NLEV/2 in integer arithmetic. It also bounds every low-level loop and separates the wind-reversal limiter from the mesosphere density limiter."
        },
        "kref": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Wave-launch (reference) level index: one above the lowest level whose height above the lowest model level reaches zref, clamped into [kgwdmin, kgwdmax]."
        },
        "komax": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Level index one above the lowest level reaching the maximum sub-grid peak ELVMAX, raised to at least kref. The flow-blocking search measures its potential energy against the height of this level."
        },
        "kbomax": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Level index one above the lowest level reaching ELVMAX + 2 var: the top of the downward flow-blocking search."
        },
        "delks": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1/Pa",
          "description": "Reciprocal of the pressure depth of the sub-column below the reference level, measured on the INTERFACES: 1/(prsi[1] - prsi[kref])."
        },
        "delks1": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1/Pa",
          "description": "Reciprocal of the same depth measured on the layer MID-POINTS: 1/(prsl[1] - prsl[kref]). The scheme uses the interface form for the momentum and density means and the mid-point form for the stability means."
        },
        "wmass": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Normalised layer-mass weights del delks of the low-level momentum and density means; they sum to one over k < kref."
        },
        "wpres": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Normalised mid-point-thickness weights (prsl[k] - prsl[k+1]) delks1 of the low-level stability means; they sum to one over k < kref. The Fortran writes the k = 1 term separately as `wtkbj` and the rest in a loop, which is the same weight evaluated at k = 1."
        },
        "ubar": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m/s",
          "description": "Mass-weighted mean earth-relative zonal wind below the reference level."
        },
        "vbar": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m/s",
          "description": "Mass-weighted mean earth-relative meridional wind below the reference level."
        },
        "rhobar": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/m^3",
          "description": "Mass-weighted mean density below the reference level."
        },
        "ulow": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m/s",
          "description": "Speed of the low-level mean wind, floored at velmin. The floor is also the calm-wind switch: ulow == velmin is one of the six conditions that turn the scheme off."
        },
        "velco_raw": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m/s",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "The projected interface wind speed before small positive values are raised to velmin: ((u[k]+u[k+1]) ubar + (v[k]+v[k+1]) vbar) / (2 ulow), zero at NLEV."
        },
        "velco": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m/s",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Wind speed at the layer INTERFACE k+1/2 projected on the low-level mean wind direction, ((u[k]+u[k+1]) ubar + (v[k]+v[k+1]) vbar) / (2 ulow). A small POSITIVE value is raised to velmin; a negative one is left alone, because its sign is what detects a critical level. Element NLEV is never defined by the Fortran (the array is declared kts:kte-1) and never read; it is set to zero here."
        },
        "usqj_raw": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Layer (gradient) Richardson number N^2/S^2 across the interface k+1/2, floored at rimin, with the squared shear floored at dw2min. Element NLEV is undefined in the Fortran and set to zero here."
        },
        "bnv2_raw": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1/s^2",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Squared Brunt-Vaisala frequency across the interface k+1/2, from the virtual potential temperature: 2 g (theta_v[k+1] - theta_v[k]) / ((theta_v[k+1] + theta_v[k]) dz_geom). Element NLEV is undefined in the Fortran and set to zero here."
        },
        "bnv2low": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1/s^2",
          "description": "Pressure-weighted mean of bnv2_raw below the reference level. The Fortran stores it back into bnv2(:,1), and its sign is the sixth off-switch: a statically unstable launch layer means no drag."
        },
        "usqjlow": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Pressure-weighted mean of usqj_raw below the reference level; the Fortran stores it back into usqj(:,1)."
        },
        "bnv2": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1/s^2",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "The N^2 profile as the later stages see it: the low-level mean at k = 1 and the raw layer value above. The flow-blocking search reads it at every level and the wave-saturation profile reads it at k >= kref, so the substitution at k = 1 reaches only the launch stress, through bnv = sqrt(bnv2[1])."
        },
        "usqj": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "The Richardson-number profile as the later stages see it: the low-level mean flooded through every level below kref, and the raw layer value at and above kref. Only the k >= kref part reaches the wave-saturation branch."
        },
        "nbad": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Number of levels strictly between the second and the reference level at which the projected wind is non-positive (a critical level) or the stratification is unstable. Any such level switches the scheme off."
        },
        "ldrag": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "The scheme's off switch, 1 when NO drag is computed in this column and 0 otherwise. Six conditions in OR: the sub-grid peak is below hmt_min (50 m, the ELVMAX condition of FORTRAN_BUGS B17); the sub-grid standard deviation is not positive; the projected wind is non-positive at the lowest interface; the low-level wind is calm (ulow at its floor); some level below the reference level has a critical level or unstable stratification; or the low-level mean N^2 is not positive. The daytime mixed layer of the reference run trips the fifth and sixth conditions, which is why GWDO is almost entirely off there."
        }
      },
      "equations": [
        {
          "lhs": "uproj",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "input_uproj",
            "args": []
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "vproj",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "input_vproj",
            "args": []
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "T",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "input_T",
            "args": []
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "qv",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "input_qv",
            "args": []
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "prsi",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "input_prsi",
            "args": []
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "prsl",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "input_prsl",
            "args": []
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "prslk",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "input_prslk",
            "args": []
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "zl",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "input_zl",
            "args": []
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "sina",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "input_sina",
            "args": []
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "cosa",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "input_cosa",
            "args": []
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "var",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "input_var",
            "args": []
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "omax",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "input_omax",
            "args": []
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "ze",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "-",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "index",
                    "args": [
                      "prsi",
                      1
                    ]
                  },
                  "prsi"
                ]
              },
              "wrf.g"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "zc",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "column_cell_center",
            "bindings": {
              "ze": "ze"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "dz",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "column_cell_thickness",
            "bindings": {
              "ze": "ze"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "del",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              "wrf.g",
              "dz"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "vtj",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              "T",
              {
                "op": "+",
                "args": [
                  1.0,
                  {
                    "op": "*",
                    "args": [
                      "wrf.ep_1",
                      "qv"
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "vtk",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
              "vtj",
              "prslk"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "rho",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
              "prsl",
              {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  "wrf.r_d",
                  "vtj"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "u1",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "-",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  "uproj",
                  "cosa"
                ]
              },
              {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  "vproj",
                  "sina"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "v1",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "+",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  "uproj",
                  "sina"
                ]
              },
              {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  "vproj",
                  "cosa"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "dzg",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "faq",
            "output_idx": [
              "k"
            ],
            "args": [
              "zl"
            ],
            "ranges": {
              "k": {
                "from": "lev"
              }
            },
            "expr": {
              "op": "ifelse",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "<",
                  "args": [
                    "k",
                    "NLEV"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "op": "-",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "index",
                      "args": [
                        "zl",
                        {
                          "op": "+",
                          "args": [
                            "k",
                            1
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "op": "index",
                      "args": [
                        "zl",
                        "k"
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                1.0
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "dw2",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "faq",
            "output_idx": [
              "k"
            ],
            "args": [
              "u1",
              "v1"
            ],
            "ranges": {
              "k": {
                "from": "lev"
              }
            },
            "expr": {
              "op": "ifelse",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "<",
                  "args": [
                    "k",
                    "NLEV"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "op": "+",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "^",
                      "args": [
                        {
                          "op": "-",
                          "args": [
                            {
                              "op": "index",
                              "args": [
                                "u1",
                                "k"
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "op": "index",
                              "args": [
                                "u1",
                                {
                                  "op": "+",
                                  "args": [
                                    "k",
                                    1
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        2
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "op": "^",
                      "args": [
                        {
                          "op": "-",
                          "args": [
                            {
                              "op": "index",
                              "args": [
                                "v1",
                                "k"
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "op": "index",
                              "args": [
                                "v1",
                                {
                                  "op": "+",
                                  "args": [
                                    "k",
                                    1
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        2
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                0.0
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "zref",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              2.0,
              "var"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "kgwdmax",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "floor",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "/",
                "args": [
                  "NLEV",
                  2
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "kref",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "max",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "min",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "apply_expression_template",
                    "args": [],
                    "name": "level_index_above",
                    "bindings": {
                      "z": {
                        "op": "-",
                        "args": [
                          "zl",
                          {
